      {
        "title": "Year 1–3 Property Strategy",
        "body": "The first three years establish the economic foundation for the rest of the match. Prioritise buying all properties in your starting region before moving to other areas—a monopoly on even one region's properties generates rent income that compounds. Never spend Nozomi Card turns on stations with fewer than 10 properties in your starting area; the transit time cost outweighs the goal bonus until year 5. Budget at least 50 million yen in reserve at all times to cover a Bomberman property loss."
      },
      {
        "title": "Card Usage Fundamentals",
        "body": "Cards are the primary variable that separates winners from losers in competitive Momotetsu. General usage hierarchy: Milk Card (hold until needed for debt crisis) > Hero Card (use against Bomberman within 3 spaces) > Nozomi Card (reserve for 10+ year long-distance goals) > Kintaro Card (bonus amplifier for high-value arrivals). Never use Nozomi and Kintaro Cards in the same turn—the Nozomi Card provides free transit but does not amplify the Kintaro arrival bonus."
      }
    ]
