      {
        "title": "Bomberman Event Management",
        "body": "Bomberman steals properties when he lands on your stations—the probability of landing increases when you own many consecutive stations along a train line. Counter-strategy: buy properties on different train lines rather than clustering on a single line. If Bomberman has been a persistent issue, keep a Hero Card ready and activate it when Bomberman is within 3–5 spaces of your highest-value station cluster. Selling low-value properties before Bomberman arrives reduces potential losses at the cost of future income."
      },
      {
        "title": "Station Purchase Timing",
        "body": "Premium stations (Tokyo, Osaka, Sapporo mega-stations) become available at different years based on match length—longer matches (60+ year mode) see premium stations available by year 15–20. Purchase one share of premium stations as soon as available, as their value compounds with each passing year. The Kyushu Loop route (Fukuoka → Nagasaki → Kumamoto → Kagoshima) provides the best mid-value station density for a single pass purchase loop in years 8–15."
      }
